      "text": "First, apply the distributive property using the equation $23^2 + 2\\cdot23\\cdot2 + 2^2 = (23^1 + 1)(23)^1 + 2^2$:\n$(23 + 1)(23) + 2^2 = 24(23) + 2^2$.\n\nNext, square $24$:\n$24(23) + 2^2 = 24(23) + 2^2 = 552 + 2^2$.\n\nThen, express $2^2$ as $(2^1)(2^1)$:\n$552 + 2^2 = 552 + (2^1)(2^1) = 552 + 2^1(2^1)$.\n\nNow, square $2^2$:\n$552 + 2^2 = 552 + (2^1)(2^1) = 552 + 2^2$.\n\nFinally, express $2^1(2^1)$ as $2^1(2^1) = 2^2$:\n$552 + 2^2 = 552 + 2^2 = \\boxed{578}$.\n\nProblem Statement:\nWhat is the value of $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$?\n\nSolution Steps:\nBefore solving this expression, start by applying the distributive property using the equation $23^2 + 2\\cdot23\\cdot2 + 2^2 = (23^1 + 1)(23)^1 + 2^2$:\n$(23 + 1)(23) + 2^2 = 24(23) + 2^2$.\n\nNext, square $24$:\n$24(23) + 2^2 = 552 + 2^2 = 552 + 2^2 = 554$.\n\nNow, square $2^2$:\n$554 + 2^2 = 554 + 2^2 = 552 + 2^2 = 578$.\n\nThus, the value of $23^2 + 2(23)(2) + 2^2$ is $\\boxed{578}$.",
